layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /overhead/
title: Overhead · live aircraft near Largs
heading: Overhead
subtitle: What's flying near Largs right now — every aircraft broadcasting its position within twenty nautical miles (about 23 miles) of the town.
---
{# Live aircraft identifier, v1.1 (map first, per Ian's ruling 19 Aug).
   Order: stamp and intro (the honesty framing precedes the picture),
   then the map, then the cards. Clicking a plane opens a popup with the
   short version and a "full details" anchor down to its card, which
   flashes via :target.

   Data path: polls /api/overhead (functions/api/overhead.js) every 8 s
   while visible; one shared edge snapshot keeps the whole town at ≤ ~7
   upstream requests a minute.

   ROUTES (live from v1.2): the function attaches
   `route: { iata: "LHR-GLA", from: "London Heathrow", to: "Glasgow" }`
   from a cached adsbdb.com lookup of the callsign — airline flights
   only, and only when the lookup answers. Cards render the names, map
   popups the codes. Contract in functions/api/overhead.js.

   ROTORCRAFT (v1.3): category A7 — the aircraft's own declaration — or a
   known helicopter type code swaps the map glyph for a rotor disc.
   Neither signal present: plane glyph, card text still only what's
   known. #}

<section class="board wrap" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="kicker">
    <span class="stamp" id="ac-stamp">Live positions — loading…</span>
  </div>

  <p class="page-intro">Aircraft broadcast their own position, height and
  callsign every second (a system called ADS&#8209;B); volunteer receivers
  across the country collect it, and this page shows everything heard
  within twenty nautical miles of Largs — Glasgow and Prestwick traffic,
  the Coastguard helicopter, transatlantic flights crossing high overhead.
  Tap a plane on the map for the short version; the cards below have the
  detail, <strong>closest first</strong>. Where a flight's usual route is
  known it's shown too — that comes from a community lookup of the
  callsign, not the aircraft itself, so it appears only when it checks
  out. Not everything flying appears: some military and light aircraft
  don't broadcast, so this is what's transmitting, not a complete picture
  of the sky.</p>

  <noscript><p class="page-intro"><strong>This page needs JavaScript</strong> —
  the positions update live, several times a minute, which a static page
  can't do. Everything else on the site works without it.</p></noscript>

  <div id="ac-map" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <ol class="ac-list" id="ac-list" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Aircraft currently overhead, closest first"></ol>
  <p class="ac-empty" id="ac-empty" hidden>Nothing broadcasting within twenty
  nautical miles just now — the quiet sky is also an answer.</p>
  <p class="ac-down" id="ac-down" hidden>Live aircraft data is unavailable at
  the moment. It comes from community-run receivers and will return when
  their feed does.</p>

  <p class="ac-credit">Aircraft data from
  <a href="https://adsb.lol">adsb.lol</a> — a community network of
  volunteer receivers, open data (ODbL). This site runs its own receiver
  station, which fetches the Largs picture from that network and relays
  it here. Positions are as broadcast by the aircraft themselves; route
  lookups via <a href="https://www.adsbdb.com">adsbdb</a>.
  Map © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a>
  contributors.</p>
</section>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.css">
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.js"></script>

<style>
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    html{scroll-behavior:auto}
  }
  .ac-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 22px;display:grid;gap:10px}
  .ac-row{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--sand);border-radius:10px;
    padding:11px 16px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px 14px;align-items:baseline}
  .ac-row:target{outline:3px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:2px}
  .ac-who{font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem}
  .ac-type{color:var(--teal);font-weight:500}
  .ac-type-unknown{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;font-style:italic}
  .ac-where{width:100%;color:var(--ink)}
  .ac-where .ac-meta{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
  .ac-route{color:var(--slate);font-weight:500}
  .ac-tag{font-size:.78rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--warn);border:1px solid var(--warn);border-radius:6px;padding:0 6px}
  .ac-tag-ground{color:var(--muted);border-color:var(--muted)}
  .ac-stale .ac-who,.ac-stale .ac-type{color:var(--muted)}
  .ac-empty,.ac-down{margin:18px 0;color:var(--muted);font-style:italic}
  #ac-map{height:400px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--sand);margin:8px 0 4px}
  .ac-credit{color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem;margin:10px 0 26px}
  .ac-plane{color:var(--slate)}
  .ac-more{width:100%;margin-top:6px}
  .ac-more summary{
    font-size:.86rem;color:var(--teal);cursor:pointer;
    list-style:none;display:inline-block;
  }
  .ac-more summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  .ac-more summary::before{content:"▸ ";font-size:.8em}
  .ac-more[open] summary::before{content:"▾ "}
  .ac-more dl{
    display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:2px 14px;
    margin:6px 0 2px;font-size:.9rem;
  }
  .ac-more dt{color:var(--muted)}
  .ac-more dd{color:var(--ink)}
  .ac-pop strong{font-size:1rem}
  .ac-pop a{color:var(--teal)}
</style>

<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";

  var HOME = [55.795, -4.87];
  var POLL_MS = 5000;

  // Friendly names for the type codes Largs actually sees. Anything not
  // listed shows its raw ICAO code — honest, and the table grows on request.
  var TYPES = {
    A319:"Airbus A319", A320:"Airbus A320", A321:"Airbus A321",
    A19N:"Airbus A319neo", A20N:"Airbus A320neo", A21N:"Airbus A321neo",
    A332:"Airbus A330-200", A333:"Airbus A330-300", A339:"Airbus A330-900neo",
    A343:"Airbus A340-300", A359:"Airbus A350-900", A35K:"Airbus A350-1000",
    A388:"Airbus A380", A400:"Airbus A400M Atlas",
    B737:"Boeing 737-700", B738:"Boeing 737-800", B38M:"Boeing 737 MAX 8",
    B39M:"Boeing 737 MAX 9", B744:"Boeing 747-400", B748:"Boeing 747-8",
    B752:"Boeing 757-200", B763:"Boeing 767-300", B772:"Boeing 777-200",
    B77L:"Boeing 777-200LR", B77W:"Boeing 777-300ER",
    B788:"Boeing 787-8", B789:"Boeing 787-9", B78X:"Boeing 787-10",
    E145:"Embraer 145", E170:"Embraer 170", E75L:"Embraer 175",
    E190:"Embraer 190", E195:"Embraer 195",
    AT46:"ATR 42-600", AT76:"ATR 72-600", DH8D:"Dash 8 Q400",
    JS41:"Jetstream 41", SB20:"Saab 2000",
    C130:"C-130 Hercules", C30J:"C-130J Super Hercules", P8:"P-8 Poseidon",
    EUFI:"Typhoon", F35:"F-35 Lightning", HAWK:"Hawk",
    EC35:"EC135 helicopter", EC45:"EC145 helicopter", EC55:"EC155 helicopter",
    A109:"AW109 helicopter", A139:"AW139 helicopter", A169:"AW169 helicopter",
    A101:"Merlin helicopter", S76:"Sikorsky S-76 helicopter",
    S92:"Sikorsky S-92 helicopter", B06:"Bell 206 helicopter",
    B429:"Bell 429 helicopter", H47:"Chinook", H60:"Black Hawk",
    R44:"Robinson R44 helicopter", R66:"Robinson R66 helicopter",
    C152:"Cessna 152", C172:"Cessna 172", C182:"Cessna 182",
    P28A:"Piper PA-28", PA28:"Piper PA-28", SR22:"Cirrus SR22",
    DA40:"Diamond DA40", DA42:"Diamond DA42",
    BE20:"King Air 200", PC12:"Pilatus PC-12", TBM9:"TBM 900"
  };

  var OPERATORS = {
    BAW:"British Airways", SHT:"British Airways", EZY:"easyJet",
    RYR:"Ryanair", RUK:"Ryanair UK", LOG:"Loganair", EXS:"Jet2",
    TOM:"TUI", VIR:"Virgin Atlantic", EIN:"Aer Lingus", KLM:"KLM",
    AFR:"Air France", DLH:"Lufthansa", SAS:"SAS", ICE:"Icelandair",
    NOS:"Norwegian", AAL:"American Airlines", UAL:"United", DAL:"Delta",
    ACA:"Air Canada", WJA:"WestJet", UPS:"UPS", FDX:"FedEx",
    GTI:"Atlas Air", CLX:"Cargolux", RRR:"Royal Air Force",
    ASY:"Royal Australian Air Force", CFC:"Canadian Forces", CNV:"US Navy",
    RCH:"US Air Force", NPT:"West Atlantic", HLE:"Helimed", CG:"Coastguard"
  };

  // Rotorcraft: ADS-B category A7 is the aircraft declaring itself a
  // rotorcraft; the type set catches transponders that omit category.
  var HELI_TYPES = { EC35:1, EC45:1, EC55:1, EC30:1, A109:1, A119:1,
    A139:1, A149:1, A169:1, A189:1, A101:1, S61:1, S76:1, S92:1,
    R22:1, R44:1, R66:1, B06:1, B212:1, B412:1, B429:1, B505:1,
    AS32:1, AS50:1, AS55:1, AS65:1, H47:1, H60:1, LYNX:1 };

  function isHeli(a) {
    return a.category === "A7" || (a.t && HELI_TYPES[a.t] === 1);
  }

  var COMPASS = ["north","north-north-east","north-east","east-north-east",
    "east","east-south-east","south-east","south-south-east","south",
    "south-south-west","south-west","west-south-west","west",
    "west-north-west","north-west","north-north-west"];

  var listEl = document.getElementById("ac-list");
  var stampEl = document.getElementById("ac-stamp");
  var emptyEl = document.getElementById("ac-empty");
  var downEl = document.getElementById("ac-down");

  var map = L.map("ac-map", { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView(HOME, 9);
  L.tileLayer("https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png", {
    maxZoom: 12,
    attribution: "&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors"
  }).addTo(map);
  L.circleMarker(HOME, { radius: 5, color: "#25655C", fillOpacity: 0.9 })
    .addTo(map).bindPopup("Largs");

  var markers = {}; // hex -> Leaflet marker
  var trails = {};  // hex -> { line: Leaflet polyline, pts: [[lat,lon], …] }
  var TRAIL_MAX = 72; // ~6 minutes of history at a 5 s cadence

  // Trails are built here, in the browser, from the positions this page
  // has already seen — no stored history, no extra requests, nothing to
  // keep. They start empty when the page opens and grow as you watch.
  function updateTrail(a) {
    var t = trails[a.hex];
    if (!t) {
      t = trails[a.hex] = {
        pts: [],
        // --rain (#5B87BC): the palette's saturated blue, chosen over
        // slate so the track reads over both land and water.
        line: L.polyline([], {
          color: "#5B87BC", weight: 3, opacity: 0.85, interactive: false
        }).addTo(map)
      };
    }
    var last = t.pts[t.pts.length - 1];
    if (!last || last[0] !== a.lat || last[1] !== a.lon) {
      t.pts.push([a.lat, a.lon]);
      if (t.pts.length > TRAIL_MAX) t.pts.shift();
      t.line.setLatLngs(t.pts);
    }
  }
  function dropTrail(hex) {
    if (!trails[hex]) return;
    map.removeLayer(trails[hex].line);
    delete trails[hex];
  }

  function planeIcon(track) {
    var deg = (typeof track === "number") ? track : 0;
    return L.divIcon({
      className: "ac-plane",
      iconSize: [26, 26],
      iconAnchor: [13, 13],
      html: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" ' +
        'style="transform:rotate(' + deg + 'deg)">' +
        '<path fill="#17333A" d="M12 1.5 14 9l8 4v2l-8-1.5V19l2.5 2V22.5L12 21l-4.5 1.5V21L10 19v-5.5L2 15v-2l8-4z"/></svg>'
    });
  }

  function heliIcon(track) {
    var deg = (typeof track === "number") ? track : 0;
    return L.divIcon({
      className: "ac-plane",
      iconSize: [26, 26],
      iconAnchor: [13, 13],
      html: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" ' +
        'style="transform:rotate(' + deg + 'deg)">' +
        '<circle cx="12" cy="10" r="7.6" fill="none" stroke="#17333A" stroke-width="1.4"/>' +
        '<line x1="6.9" y1="4.9" x2="17.1" y2="15.1" stroke="#17333A" stroke-width="1.4"/>' +
        '<line x1="17.1" y1="4.9" x2="6.9" y2="15.1" stroke="#17333A" stroke-width="1.4"/>' +
        '<ellipse cx="12" cy="10" rx="2.4" ry="3.6" fill="#17333A"/>' +
        '<rect x="11.35" y="13" width="1.3" height="7.2" rx="0.6" fill="#17333A"/>' +
        '<rect x="9.6" y="19.6" width="4.8" height="1.5" rx="0.7" fill="#17333A"/></svg>'
    });
  }

  function operatorFor(callsign) {
    var m = callsign.match(/^[A-Z]{2,3}/);
    return (m && OPERATORS[m[0]]) || null;
  }

  function feet(n) { return n.toLocaleString("en-GB") + " ft"; }
  function compass(deg) {
    return COMPASS[Math.round(((deg % 360) + 360) % 360 / 22.5) % 16];
  }
  function degStr(deg) { return Math.round(((deg % 360) + 360) % 360) + "\u00B0"; }

  // The extra fields the aircraft is already broadcasting, shown only
  // when present. Squawk is reported plainly, as a number: this page
  // records what is transmitted and does not dramatise it.
  function detailRows(a) {
    var rows = [];
    if (typeof a.track === "number") {
      rows.push(["Heading", compass(a.track) + " (" + degStr(a.track) + ")"]);
    }
    if (typeof a.baro_rate === "number" && Math.abs(a.baro_rate) >= 100) {
      rows.push(["Vertical rate",
        Math.abs(a.baro_rate).toLocaleString("en-GB") + " ft/min " +
        (a.baro_rate > 0 ? "climb" : "descent")]);
    }
    if (typeof a.nav_altitude_mcp === "number") {
      rows.push(["Selected altitude", feet(a.nav_altitude_mcp)]);
    }
    var sp = [];
    if (typeof a.gs === "number") sp.push(mph(a.gs) + " over the ground");
    if (typeof a.mach === "number") sp.push("Mach " + a.mach.toFixed(2));
    if (sp.length) rows.push(["Speed", sp.join(" \u00B7 ")]);
    if (typeof a.ws === "number" && typeof a.wd === "number") {
      rows.push(["Wind aloft",
        Math.round(a.ws) + " kt from " + compass(a.wd) + " (" + degStr(a.wd) + ")"]);
    }
    if (typeof a.oat === "number") {
      rows.push(["Air temperature", Math.round(a.oat) + "\u00B0C"]);
    }
    if (a.squawk) rows.push(["Squawk", String(a.squawk)]);
    if (a.r) rows.push(["Registration", a.r]);
    return rows;
  }
  function mph(kn) { return Math.round(kn * 1.151).toLocaleString("en-GB") + " mph"; }
  function milesOf(nm) { return (nm * 1.1508).toFixed(nm < 4.5 ? 1 : 0); }

  function whoOf(a) {
    var callsign = (a.flight || "").trim();
    var who = callsign || a.r || a.hex.toUpperCase();
    var op = callsign ? operatorFor(callsign) : null;
    return op ? op + " " + who : who;
  }

  function routeParts(a) {
    return (a.route && a.route.from && a.route.to) ? a.route : null;
  }

  function rowFor(a) {
    var callsign = (a.flight || "").trim();
    var onGround = a.alt_baro === "ground";
    var military = (a.dbFlags || 0) & 1;

    var li = document.createElement("li");
    li.id = "ac-" + a.hex;
    li.className = "ac-row" + ((a.seen_pos || 0) > 30 ? " ac-stale" : "");

    var whoEl = document.createElement("span");
    whoEl.className = "ac-who";
    whoEl.textContent = whoOf(a);
    li.appendChild(whoEl);

    var typeEl = document.createElement("span");
    typeEl.className = a.t ? "ac-type" : "ac-type ac-type-unknown";
    typeEl.textContent = a.t ? (TYPES[a.t] || a.t) : "type unknown";
    li.appendChild(typeEl);

    if (military) {
      var tag = document.createElement("span");
      tag.className = "ac-tag";
      tag.textContent = "military";
      li.appendChild(tag);
    }
    if (onGround) {
      var g = document.createElement("span");
      g.className = "ac-tag ac-tag-ground";
      g.textContent = "on the ground";
      li.appendChild(g);
    }

    // one line carries the story: route (when known) · position · height
    // · speed · registration · staleness
    var where = document.createElement("span");
    where.className = "ac-where";

    var rp = routeParts(a);
    if (rp) {
      var routeEl = document.createElement("span");
      routeEl.className = "ac-route";
      routeEl.textContent = rp.from + " → " + rp.to;
      where.appendChild(routeEl);
      where.appendChild(document.createTextNode(" · "));
    }

    var dir = COMPASS[Math.round(((a.dir || 0) % 360) / 22.5) % 16];
    var main = onGround
      ? milesOf(a.dst || 0) + " miles " + dir + " of Largs"
      : milesOf(a.dst || 0) + " miles " + dir + " of Largs · " + feet(a.alt_baro) +
        ((a.baro_rate || 0) > 300 ? ", climbing" : (a.baro_rate || 0) < -300 ? ", descending" : "");
    where.appendChild(document.createTextNode(main));

    var bits = [];
    if (typeof a.gs === "number" && !onGround) bits.push(mph(a.gs));
    if (a.r && callsign) bits.push(a.r);
    if ((a.seen_pos || 0) > 30) bits.push("position " + Math.round(a.seen_pos) + "s old");
    if (bits.length) {
      var meta = document.createElement("span");
      meta.className = "ac-meta";
      meta.textContent = " · " + bits.join(" · ");
      where.appendChild(meta);
    }
    li.appendChild(where);

    var rows = detailRows(a);
    if (rows.length) {
      var det = document.createElement("details");
      det.className = "ac-more";
      var sum = document.createElement("summary");
      sum.textContent = "More detail";
      det.appendChild(sum);
      var dl = document.createElement("dl");
      rows.forEach(function (r) {
        var dt = document.createElement("dt");
        dt.textContent = r[0];
        var dd = document.createElement("dd");
        dd.textContent = r[1];
        dl.appendChild(dt);
        dl.appendChild(dd);
      });
      det.appendChild(dl);
      li.appendChild(det);
    }

    return li;
  }

  function popupFor(a) {
    var onGround = a.alt_baro === "ground";
    var div = document.createElement("div");
    div.className = "ac-pop";
    var s = document.createElement("strong");
    s.textContent = whoOf(a);
    div.appendChild(s);
    var lines = [];
    lines.push(a.t ? (TYPES[a.t] || a.t) : "type unknown");
    var rp = routeParts(a);
    if (rp) lines.push((rp.iata || "").replace("-", " → "));
    if (!onGround) {
      lines.push(feet(a.alt_baro) + (typeof a.gs === "number" ? " · " + mph(a.gs) : ""));
    } else {
      lines.push("on the ground");
    }
    lines.forEach(function (t) {
      div.appendChild(document.createElement("br"));
      div.appendChild(document.createTextNode(t));
    });
    div.appendChild(document.createElement("br"));
    var link = document.createElement("a");
    link.href = "#ac-" + a.hex;
    link.textContent = "full details ↓";
    div.appendChild(link);
    return div;
  }

  function render(data, staleHeader) {
    var ac = (data.ac || []).filter(function (a) {
      return typeof a.lat === "number" && typeof a.lon === "number";
    });
    ac.sort(function (x, y) {
      var gx = x.alt_baro === "ground" ? 1 : 0;
      var gy = y.alt_baro === "ground" ? 1 : 0;
      return gx - gy || (x.dst || 99) - (y.dst || 99);
    });

    listEl.textContent = "";
    ac.forEach(function (a) { listEl.appendChild(rowFor(a)); });
    emptyEl.hidden = ac.length !== 0;
    downEl.hidden = true;

    var seen = {};
    ac.forEach(function (a) {
      seen[a.hex] = true;
      var pos = [a.lat, a.lon];
      updateTrail(a);
      var icon = (isHeli(a) ? heliIcon : planeIcon)(a.track);
      if (markers[a.hex]) {
        markers[a.hex].setLatLng(pos).setIcon(icon);
      } else {
        markers[a.hex] = L.marker(pos, { icon: icon }).addTo(map);
        markers[a.hex].bindPopup("");
      }
      markers[a.hex].getPopup().setContent(popupFor(a));
    });
    Object.keys(markers).forEach(function (hex) {
      if (!seen[hex]) { map.removeLayer(markers[hex]); delete markers[hex]; }
    });
    Object.keys(trails).forEach(function (hex) {
      if (!seen[hex]) dropTrail(hex);
    });

    var when = data.now ? new Date(data.now) : new Date();
    var hhmmss = when.toLocaleTimeString("en-GB");
    var age = data.now ? Math.round((Date.now() - data.now) / 1000) : 0;
    stampEl.textContent = "Positions as of " + hhmmss +
      (staleHeader || age > 30 ? " — feed interrupted, showing last received" : "") +
      " · updates every 5 seconds while this page is open";
  }

  function showDown() {
    listEl.textContent = "";
    Object.keys(markers).forEach(function (hex) {
      map.removeLayer(markers[hex]); delete markers[hex];
    });
    Object.keys(trails).forEach(dropTrail);
    emptyEl.hidden = true;
    downEl.hidden = false;
    stampEl.textContent = "Live positions unavailable";
  }

  var failures = 0;
  function poll() {
    fetch("/api/overhead")
      .then(function (r) {
        if (r.status === 503) throw new Error("unavailable");
        var stale = r.headers.get("x-overhead-stale") === "1";
        return r.json().then(function (d) {
          if (d.unavailable) throw new Error("unavailable");
          failures = 0;
          render(d, stale);
        });
      })
      .catch(function () {
        failures += 1;
        if (failures >= 3) showDown();
      });
  }

  var timer = null;
  function start() { if (!timer) { poll(); timer = setInterval(poll, POLL_MS); } }
  function stop() { if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; } }

  document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", function () {
    if (document.hidden) { stop(); } else { start(); }
  });
  start();
})();
</script>
